# [KEYTRANS](../wg/keytrans.html)

## Summary

The KEYTRANS Working Group met at IETF 120 to discuss the status of its core documents, updates to the protocol specification, and insights from recent client implementations. The Architecture document has been submitted to the IESG for publication, with Corey serving as the document shepherd. Brendan McMillion presented significant updates to [draft-ietf-keytrans-protocol](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-keytrans-protocol), covering wire formats, third-party management, and credentials. Felix Linker presented feedback and findings from a Rust-based client implementation effort, highlighting areas of complexity in the specification's tree structures and calling for a clearer path toward wire-format interoperability.

